Content Discovery: involves things that are not immediately presented and not destined for public access.
Major procedures for used during content discovery include:
i. Manual
ii. OSINT(Open Source Intelligence)
iii. Automated

Manual Discovery: Involves visually observing and scanning the Web page for potential loopholes that might have been overlooked by the
Web Developer.
 Some of the methods include 
Favicon: Every established webpage will always have a favicon (small icon at the top of page, like a website logo). This favicon will 
always contain an hash value(md5sum format) that can be looked up on a certain website that can provide more information about the documenting
and tools used to create the site.

